            "review_title": "Review at Grandma Vượng’s Charcuterie & Bánh Mì Bakery",
            "review_text": "Imro\nAmsterdam157 contributions\n0\nExcellent banh mi - homemade pate and meats!\nAug 2025 • Family\nLooking for a great Banh Mi? Look no further because Grandma Vượng’s has you covered.\n\nWe stayed in Hoi An and Da Nang for few days and were craving a good banh mi - as there are many options we decided to pick a spot we saw on TikTok and liked the story, interiour, ac and also the authentic choice of fillings.\n\nCame in around 19.00 on tuesday and were greeted immediatly by aunty Hannah and later also the other owner, the son, came in and he made us a nice sugarcane juice.\n\nWe ordered a Hanoi and Saigon style and it was amazing. We enjoyed the inhouse made ham and sausage. Something unique and this sets the shop apart. There is also an option to add egg or brie.\n\nAs we were heading out we chatted a bit waiting for our grab and the story and history were shared and we even got a look at were the ham and sausages are being made! Homemade is not a buzzword here.\n\nall in all highly recommended and truly a unique experience and very very friendly owners where you can tell how proud they are and righfully so!\nRead more\nWritten August 5, 2025\nEric T\nIt was such a joy meeting you, your wife, and your daughter, and hearing your story as well. Grandma Hannah and I felt truly touched seeing how much you all appreciated visiting our kitchen where we craft our charcuterie. I also genuinely enjoyed being part of your daughter’s YouTube video—it was such a special experience. We sincerely hope our paths cross again someday, and we look forward to welcoming you back.\nRead more\nWritten August 5, 2025\nThis response is the subjective opinion of the management representative and not of Tripadvisor LLC nor of its partners.",
